# ============================================================================
# PUSH-WHITELIST for GitHub Pages (inverted logic: everything is ignored
# EXCEPT what the published game needs). GitHub Pages serves the repo as-is,
# so only true game files may be pushed - nothing else.
#
# The game online needs exactly:
#   index.html, main.js, animations/, audio/, css/, images/, js/ and
#   generated/phase2/entry.mjs (index.html loads exactly this ONE file;
#   it contains the whole game). .nojekyll (stops GitHub's
#   site builder from skipping underscore files like animations/Stox/abilities/_shared)
#
# The repo WORKFLOW files (package.json, eslint config, tools/, dev/tests/,
# .github/) are also committed - they are needed for the full
# lint + tests + phase2:verify + build gate on GitHub, are never loaded by
# the game, and add nothing secret to GitHub Pages. Everything else (docs,
# notes, art sources, previews, other dev/ scratch) stays local-only.
# ============================================================================

# --- ignore everything, then allow the game back in ---
/*

# --- the published game ---
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/index.html
!/main.js
!/animations/
!/audio/
!/css/
!/images/
!/js/
!/generated/

# --- generated/: ONLY entry.mjs is loaded by index.html (verified: nothing
# --- in the game fetches order.json / manifest-imports.json - those are
# --- build-tool bookkeeping and stay local-only) ---
/generated/*
!/generated/phase2/
/generated/phase2/*
!/generated/phase2/entry.mjs

# --- repo workflow: lint / tests / phase2 build / GitHub CI ---
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/eslint.config.js
!/README.md
!/.github/
!/tools/
!/dev/
# dev/ stays local-only EXCEPT its tests, which CI runs.
/dev/*
!/dev/tests/

# --- junk that must never be pushed even from allowed folders ---
node_modules/
dist/
**/~$*
*.pid
.preview_server.pid
.eslintcache
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
shots/
